@startuml
title Option A — normal critical delivery via push
hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
actor "Bank service\nproducer outbox" as Producer
participant "Notification API" as API
database "PostgreSQL\nledger + outbox" as DB
participant "Outbox relay" as Relay
queue "Kafka\ncritical topics" as Kafka
participant "Orchestrator" as FSM
participant "Push worker" as Worker
participant "FCM / APNs" as Push
actor "Bank app" as App
participant "Receipt Gateway" as Receipt

Producer -> API: Submit(logical_key, event, user)
API -> DB: BEGIN; unique inbox; notification; outbox; COMMIT
DB --> API: Synchronous durable commit
API --> Producer: 202 Accepted(notification_id)
note over API, DB: 202 means durable acceptance, not device delivery.
Relay -> DB: Claim unpublished outbox
Relay -> Kafka: Publish notification_id
Kafka -> FSM: Deliver event (duplicates possible)
FSM -> DB: Dedup inbox + select eligible route\ncreate PUSH attempt + deadline t0+8s + command outbox
Relay -> Kafka: Publish attempt command
Kafka -> Worker: attempt_id
Worker -> DB: Claim attempt; verify current state / preference version
Worker -> Push: Send(notification_id, attempt_id, TTL=8s)
Push --> Worker: Provider accepted + message_id
Worker -> DB: Record accepted; wait for receipt
Push -> App: Push message
App -> App: Persistent dedup by notification_id
App -> Receipt: Authenticated received ACK(notification_id)
Receipt -> DB: Receipt inbox + CAS DELIVERED\ncancel unsent future attempts; outbox; COMMIT
note over DB, Receipt: App receipt is delivery evidence; opening / reading is separate.
note over Producer, Kafka: Crash after COMMIT or duplicate publication is recovered by outbox + inbox.
@enduml
